The first implemented adapter, XiaomiRemoteBridgeMac, is a macOS adaptation
informed by the GPL-3.0 project:
https://github.com/xxb26553663-star/remote-bridge-hub

Reference revision:
8a93f321ac71a602300c6cd77f7256fa4b63068e

Changes include a native SwiftUI menu bar host, CoreBluetooth state machine,
CoreAudio output selection, IOHID permission gating, macOS key injection,
packaging, and macOS-focused tests. The adapted work is distributed under
GPL-3.0-only. See LICENSE and THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.

A Windows source/build candidate for the same device, apps/windows/rc003,
is a clean-room Python reimplementation informed by reading (read-only) the
same GPL-3.0 reference project and revision above. It does not copy any
upstream source lines; it reuses only interoperability facts (GATT UUIDs,
control opcodes, IMA/DVI ADPCM tables, HID usage IDs, VID/PID values). It
does not include the upstream VB-CABLE packaging, Frida injection, other
device bridges (T1/V60), or commercial branding. See
apps/windows/rc003/ATTRIBUTION.md for the file-by-file provenance record.
This candidate has not completed real-Windows-device acceptance; see
apps/windows/rc003/README.md, in particular its "Known gaps" section.
